---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Us — PeptideLab" description="Meet Dr. Adrian Cole, PeptideLab research director, and learn about our HPLC and mass spectrometry purity verification and certificate of analysis process.">
  <section class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-lab-heading">About PeptideLab</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
      PeptideLab supplies high-purity research peptides and laboratory materials to the scientific
      community. We serve researchers, laboratories and academic institutions that require reliable,
      well-documented research compounds.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
      Every product is manufactured under controlled conditions and independently verified for purity.
      Each batch is accompanied by a certificate of analysis (CoA) so researchers can verify the quality
      of the material they receive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-lab-heading">Research Director</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-[12px] border border-lab-rule bg-lab-panel p-6">
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-medium text-lab-heading">Dr. Adrian Cole</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-lab-faint">Research Director</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
        Dr. Adrian Cole is the Research Director at PeptideLab, with a background in analytical
        biochemistry and peptide characterization. He coordinates third-party purity verification and
        batch documentation for the research catalog.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
        His expertise spans peptide chemistry, HPLC purity verification, mass spectrometry and
        lyophilization — the analytical methods used to document every batch supplied to researchers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-lab-heading">Verification Methodology</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
      Purity and identity are verified using a two-tier analytical approach that follows laboratory best
      practices consistent with methods reported in the peer-reviewed research literature.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-[12px] border border-lab-rule bg-lab-panel p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-medium text-lab-heading">HPLC Purity</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
          High-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) is used to determine the chromatographic purity
          of each batch. Research-grade material is documented at &gt;99% purity.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-[12px] border border-lab-rule bg-lab-panel p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-medium text-lab-heading">Mass Spectrometry</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
          Mass spectrometry (MS) is used as an orthogonal identity method to confirm molecular weight and
          verify the correct molecular form of the peptide.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-lab-heading">Certificate of Analysis Process</h2>
    <ol class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
      <li><strong class="text-lab-text">Batch sampling</strong> — a representative sample is taken from each produced batch.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-lab-text">HPLC purity testing</strong> — chromatographic purity is measured and recorded.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-lab-text">MS identity confirmation</strong> — molecular weight is confirmed by mass spectrometry.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-lab-text">CoA issued</strong> — purity, content, molecular weight, batch number and test date are documented on the certificate of analysis supplied with the order.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl rounded-[12px] border border-lab-rule bg-lab-panel p-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-medium text-lab-heading">Research use only</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-lab-muted">
      PeptideLab supplies products for laboratory research use only. We do not sell products for human
      or veterinary consumption, and we do not provide medical or dosing guidance.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
